{
  "slug": "tokai-no-hoshikuzu",
  "family": "tracks",
  "label": "Grand Voyage",
  "note": "original — written in the idiom of the One Piece sea-shanty, not transcribed from it or from any score. D natural minor, 6/8 at a dotted-quarter of 120 (rowLen 3675; a row is a 16th, so a bar is 12 rows and bars straddle the 32-row patterns), 32 bars over 12 patterns, loops at exactly 32 s. 4-bar brass call, A section Dm Gm C F / Dm A7 Dm A7, A' with a run up on bar 20, hook F C Dm A7 / F C Gm A7, 4-bar tag Dm Gm A7 A7 back to bar 1. 7 ch: sail_lead = the shanty (long-short lilt on the two pulses, A4-Bb5, the A tune stated twice before the hook takes it up a fourth), low_chunk = the chuck an octave down, two soft sine notes a bar on the eighth before each pulse, voiced on the chord tones sea_brass is not holding, sea_brass = the call and then the held answer in the lead's rests, rope_bass = root on pulse 1, fifth on pulse 2, an approach only where the chord moves, bass_drum_1 / snare_1 / hihat_2 = deck drum on both pulses, backbeat on pulse 2 with a 16th roll into each section, tambourine on the offbeat eighths.",
